    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nfiles\n\n### Description\n\nTrying to transfer several files to a subdirectory will result in the creation of new files within that directory while retaining the original ones.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.10.0-dev+1974-g714b07519\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. Open MiniFiles\r\n3. Create `world/` `hello.c` and `hello.h`\r\n4. Move `hello.c` and `hello.h` to `world/`\r\n5. Observe incorrect file system actions\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n\"hello.c\" and \"hello.h\" are effectively transferred to \"world/\".\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n[Screencast from 2024-01-17 15-57-43.webm](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/68ef1c96-d33a-4522-8baa-52b70b1d1d53)\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2024-01-18T06:27:44Z",
