        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> Judging by the video, you use blockwise selection to select the files. Moving files is [supposed to be done for whole lines](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/910e49d2d45e9d32c815d16cce6cea7c3b43cecf/doc/mini-files.txt#L298-L299), that is, with linewise (`V`) selection. This is because those lines are prepended with unique path index which is used to infer the move when it itself is moved.\r\n> \r\n> Does using `V` to select files prior to deleting works for you?\r\n\r\nLinewise selection work as intended. :)",
